# PROJECT: AICTE SAMPARK
## Integrated AICTE Approval Workflow Automation, Compliance Monitoring and Alert Management System

Act as a senior full-stack developer, UI/UX designer, software architect, and AI engineer.

Build a functional, polished, interactive web application prototype for the following hackathon problem statement.

**Organization:** All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE)

**Problem Statement ID:** 26262

**Problem Statement:** Integrated AICTE Approval Workflow Automation, Compliance Monitoring and Alert Management System.

The application must demonstrate how an integrated digital platform can automate approval-related administrative workflows, monitor institutional compliance, manage document validity, schedule Expert Visit Committee activities, and notify responsible stakeholders about pending and overdue actions.

This must be a working prototype, not merely a static dashboard, landing page, or collection of UI mockups.

---

# 1. CORE OBJECTIVE

Build a centralized AICTE-style approval management platform connecting:

1. Technical institutions.
2. Scrutiny officers.
3. Regional administrators.
4. Bureau officials.
5. Expert Visit Committee (EVC) coordinators.
6. Senior authorities.

The platform must provide role-specific dashboards, configurable approval workflows, document management, compliance tracking, deadline monitoring, notifications, reporting, and AI-assisted case analysis.

All approval routes, deadlines, and committee stages must be configurable according to the applicable Approval Process Handbook (APH) and authorised administrative procedures.

Do not assume that every application passes through the same stages.

The platform must preserve human oversight. AI may explain, summarise, recommend, and flag potential issues, but must not independently make statutory approval decisions or replace authorised inspections and verification.

Use synthetic demonstration data. Clearly identify all sample institutions, applications, officials, documents, deadlines, and approval records as fictional.

